svn-fw-limited-evict-control: TPM2_EvictControl rejects objects of limited hierarchies with TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, version 185, TPM2_EvictControl): "If
*objectHandle* references a Transient Object: 1. The TPM shall return
`TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES` if 1. it is in the hierarchy of `TPM_RH_NULL` or a
firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchy, or 2. the *stClear* is SET in the
object or in an ancestor key." (Part 1, "EvictControl of objects in
firmware-limited and SVN-limited hierarchies": "Objects in a firmware-limited
or SVN-limited hierarchy (including objects without
*firmwareLimited/svnLimited* SET), cannot be made persistent by
`TPM2_EvictControl()`.")

The reference returns TPM_RC_HIERARCHY + RC_EvictControl_objectHandle for an
object of a firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchy (the response code the
specification reserves for an object "not in the proper hierarchy as
determined by *auth*"). tpm-rs returns TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES +
RC_EvictControl_objectHandle, as specified; the patch changes the reference's
response code accordingly.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Context/EvictControl.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Context/EvictControl.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Context/EvictControl.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Context/EvictControl.c
@@ -34,9 +34,13 @@ TPM2_EvictControl(EvictControl_In* in  // IN: input parameter list
 
     // Objects in a firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchy cannot be made
     // persistent.
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // TPM 2.0 Part 3, TPM2_EvictControl: "The TPM shall return
+    // TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES if it is in the hierarchy of TPM_RH_NULL or a
+    // firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchy".
     if(HierarchyIsFirmwareLimited(evictObject->hierarchy)
        || HierarchyIsSvnLimited(evictObject->hierarchy))
-        return TPM_RCS_HIERARCHY + RC_EvictControl_objectHandle;
+        return TPM_RCS_ATTRIBUTES + RC_EvictControl_objectHandle;
 
     // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
     // public-only objects may be made persistent since revision 185 of Part 3
